==={{BotW|-}}===
Backflips are somersaults [[Link]] can perform to leap backwards,<ref name="BotW Ability Controls 2"/> and avoid certain [[Enemy]] attacks.<ref name="BotW Ability Controls 2"/><ref name="BotW Ta'loh Naeg"/> These attacks include horizontal and directly downward attacks. Backflips are achieved by simultaneously holding down on the ZL button, moving the left joystick downwards, and pressing X to jump. If timed correctly, Link performs a [[Perfect Dodging|Perfect Dodge]],<ref name="BotW N/A"/> and can then perform a [[Flurry Rush]]. Otherwise, Link can then follow up with a [[Jump Slash]]. In [[Ta'loh Naeg Shrine]], the [[Sheikah]] [[Monk]] [[Ta'loh Naeg]] instructs Link on how to use Backflips to avoid attacks.<ref name="BotW Ta'loh Naeg"/> However, Link can perform Backflips without needing to learn it from Ta'loh Naeg, and can unlock its entry in the [[Ability Controls]] menu after performing a Perfect Dodge of either kind.

==={{TotK|-}}===
Backflips return in {{TotK}} and function the same as before.<ref name="TotK Special Controls 2"/><ref name="TotK N/A"/><ref name="TotK Mysterious Voice"/> However, its entry in the [[Special Controls]] menu cannot be unlocked through simply performing a Perfect Dodge of either kind. Instead, Link must receive instructions from the [[Mysterious Voice]] in the [[Kyononis Shrine]] to unlock its entry.<ref name="TotK Mysterious Voice"/> [[Demon King Ganondorf]] is also able to perform Backflips to either create distance between himself and Link, or perform Perfect Dodges. He is able to do this in all three phases.

